Index,SS / Module,Feature,Test Case Name,Test Description,Meta Test Description,Speed,Mode,Memory Start Offset,Memory End Offset,Remarks,Test Steps / Procedure,Meta Test Steps / Procedure,Impacted Registers,Meta Impacted Registers,Validation / Acceptance Criteria,Meta Validation / Acceptance Criteria,Code Generation (Required / Not),Meta Headers,Meta Macros,Meta Arrays,Test Folder,Source File,IP Name
1,GPIO,Register Write-Read Verification,gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"This test validates the GPIO register block by performing two phases: (1) Reset value verification - reads each GPIO register after reset and compares the value (with bit 0 masked out) against the expected default value, skipping non-readable registers and registers flagged in the skip-reset array. (2) Write-read verification - writes six different data patterns (0xFFFFFFFF, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0xF5F5F5F5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xFFFF0000) into each writable GPIO register using the write mask, then reads back using the read mask and compares against the expected value computed from the write mask, read mask, and default value. The test targets registers gp0_gpio_8, gp0_gpio_9, and gp0_gpio_10. A soft reset check function is also defined but is disabled via conditional compilation. The test reports PASS if no default-value or write-read mismatches are detected, and FAIL otherwise.","The testcase gpio_reg_wr_rd_test performs GPIO register validation in two phases. Phase 1 (chk_rst_val): Iterates i=0..CNT-1 over addr_array[]. For each register address (MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10, etc.), skips if skip_rst_array[i]==1 or read_mask_array[i]==0x00000000. Reads data_rd=read_reg(addr), masks data=(data_rd & 0xfffffffe), compares data==default_value_array[i]. On mismatch, increments def_fail_cnt. Phase 2 (chk_rd_wr): Uses chk_val[6]={0xffffffff,0xaaaaaaaa,0x55555555,0xf5f5f5f5,0xA5A5A5A5,0xffff0000}. For each pattern j=0..5, writes write_reg(addr, data_wr & write_mask_array[i]) for each non-skipped writable register. Then reads data_rd=(read_reg(addr) & read_mask_array[i]), computes wr_n=(write_mask_array[i] ^ 0xffffffff), exp_val=((data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | (wr_n & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i])), compares data_rd==exp_val. On mismatch, increments wr_fail_cnt. Final verdict: if(def_fail_cnt > 0 || wr_fail_cnt > 0) finish(1) else finish(0). soft_reset_chk() is defined but inside #ifdef 0 block.",NA,Polling,NA,NA,"Bit 0 of each register read is masked out (ANDed with 0xFFFFFFFE) during reset value verification due to the data_in field being a live pin-level input that may not match the expected default. Registers flagged in the skip arrays are excluded from the respective test phases. The soft reset check function is disabled via conditional compilation and is not executed. The test requires the GPIO hardware block to be in its post-reset state before execution.","1. Initialize the test environment and ensure the GPIO register block is in its post-reset state.
2. For each target GPIO register (gp0_gpio_8, gp0_gpio_9, gp0_gpio_10 and others in the address array), read the current register value after reset.
3. Mask out bit 0 of the read value and compare against the expected default value for each register.
4. Record any default value mismatches.
5. For each of six test patterns (0xFFFFFFFF, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0xF5F5F5F5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xFFFF0000), write the pattern into each writable GPIO register using the appropriate write mask.
6. Read back each register using the read mask.
7. Compute the expected readback value considering the write mask, read mask, and default value for non-writable bits.
8. Compare the actual readback value against the computed expected value.
9. Record any write-read mismatches.
10. Report PASS if no mismatches were detected in either phase; report FAIL otherwise.","1. Entry: test_case() is called.
2. chk_rst_val() is invoked.
3. Loop i=0 to CNT-1: addr=addr_array[i]; if(skip_rst_array[i]==1) continue; if(read_mask_array[i]==0x00000000) continue; data_rd=read_reg(addr); data=(data_rd & 0xfffffffe); if(data==default_value_array[i]) PASS else def_fail_cnt++.
4. chk_rd_wr() is invoked.
5. chk_val[6]={0xffffffff,0xaaaaaaaa,0x55555555,0xf5f5f5f5,0xA5A5A5A5,0xffff0000}.
6. Outer loop j=0..5: data_wr=chk_val[j].
7. Write loop: write_reg(addr,(data_wr & write_mask_array[i])).
8. Read loop: data_rd=(read_reg(addr) & read_mask_array[i]); wr_n=(write_mask_array[i] ^ 0xffffffff); exp_val=((data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | (wr_n & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i])); if(data_rd==exp_val) PASS else wr_fail_cnt++.
9. Final: if(def_fail_cnt>0 || wr_fail_cnt>0) finish(1) else finish(0).
10. soft_reset_chk() inside #ifdef 0: read_reg/write_reg SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS. Never compiled.",gp0_gpio_8; gp0_gpio_9; gp0_gpio_10,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10; SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS,"PASS: All GPIO registers (gp0_gpio_8, gp0_gpio_9, gp0_gpio_10, and others) return their expected default values after reset (with bit 0 masked out), AND all six write-read pattern tests produce matching readback values when compared against the expected value computed from write mask, read mask, and default value. FAIL: Any register returns a mismatched default value, or any write-read pattern readback does not match the expected computed value.","Phase 1: PASS when (data_rd & 0xfffffffe)==default_value_array[i] for all non-skipped readable registers. FAIL when data!=default_value_array[i] -> def_fail_cnt++. Phase 2: PASS when (read_reg(addr) & read_mask_array[i])==exp_val for all patterns. FAIL when data_rd!=exp_val -> wr_fail_cnt++. Final: if(def_fail_cnt>0 || wr_fail_cnt>0) finish(1) [FAIL]; else finish(0) [PASS].",Not,"#include <stdio.h>; #include <stdlib.h>; #include ""test_common.h""; #include ""test_define.c""; #include<gpio/gpio_def.h>; #include<gpio/gpio_offset.h>","#define SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS 0x00000000; #define SOFT_RST_REG_DATA 0x00000000; #define CNT 49","const unsigned long int addr_array[49]={MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10,}; const unsigned int default_value_array[49]={GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_DEFAULT_VAL,}; const unsigned int read_mask_array[49]={GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_READ_MASK,}; const unsigned int write_mask_array[49]={GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_WRITE_MASK,}; const unsigned int skip_array[49]={0,0,0,...,1,...,0,0,0,0,}; const unsigned int skip_rst_array[49]={0,0,0,...,1,...,1,1,1,1,}; unsigned int chk_val[6]={0xffffffff,0xaaaaaaaa,0x55555555,0xf5f5f5f5,0xA5A5A5A5,0xffff0000};",TestRepo/gpio/gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"program.c, test_define.c",GPIO
2,GPIO,Level Select Interrupt Enable Verification,test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,"This test validates GPIO level-sensitive interrupt functionality for GPIO pins 8 through 39. It configures each GPIO pin in input mode with level interrupt enabled, first testing active-high level selection (level_sel=1) and then active-low level selection (level_sel=0). For each GPIO pin, the test enables the sysreg interrupt, programs the per-pin GPIO register for input mode with level interrupt, enables the group interrupt, triggers the interrupt via an SRAM write, and waits for the ISR to fire. In the ISR (Default_IRQHandler), the test verifies the interrupt raw status bit is set, checks the group interrupt status register, clears the interrupt by writing to the interrupt clear bit, verifies the clear was successful by reading back the register and comparing against the expected value 0x100001, disables the group interrupt, verifies the group interrupt status is cleared, and clears the sysreg interrupt status. The test reports PASS if no errors occurred across all 64 interrupt scenarios (32 active-high + 32 active-low).","The testcase test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en validates GPIO level-sensitive interrupt functionality. test_case(): Enables GIC IRQ 87 (GPIO0) or 88 (GPIO1). Writes MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1 with LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO0_INTR (or GPIO1). Active-high loop i=0..31: writes MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(i*4) with 0x00180000 (io_ctrl=1, level_sel=1, nedge_intr_en=1), wait_on(50), writes MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1 with (1<<i), writes 0xA0243ffc with 0xffffffff, sets int_pend=1, polls while(int_pend==1). Active-low loop i=0..31: writes MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(i*4) with 0x00100000 (io_ctrl=1, level_sel=0), writes MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1 with (1<<i), writes 0xA0243ffc with ~(wr_val), sets int_pend=1, polls. Default_IRQHandler(): reads MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(i*4), checks (rdata & 0x2)!=0x0 for raw status, reads MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1 and checks (rdata_grp & (1<<i))!=0, writes MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(i*4) with 0x00110000 to clear interrupt, reads back and checks rdata==0x100001, writes MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1 with 0x00000000, reads MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1 and checks ==0x0, writes/reads MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1 to clear sysreg status. finish(test_err).",NA,ISR,NA,NA,"GIC IRQ 87 (for GPIO0) or IRQ 88 (for GPIO1) must be available and functional. The sysreg interrupt chain must be properly configured. An SRAM location at 0xA0243ffc is used to trigger GPIO pin level changes. The test requires external hardware or testbench stimulus to drive GPIO pin levels corresponding to the programmed level_sel value. The GPIO block must be in its post-reset state before execution.","1. Enable the GIC interrupt line for the GPIO instance under test.
2. Enable the GPIO interrupt in the sysreg interrupt enable register (intr_en1).
3. For each GPIO pin (8 through 39), configure the per-pin register (gp0_gpio_8 through gp0_gpio_39) in input mode with level interrupt enabled and active-high level selection.
4. Enable the corresponding bit in the group interrupt enable register (gp0_intr1_intr_en1).
5. Trigger the interrupt by writing to the SRAM trigger location.
6. Wait for the ISR to fire and verify: the interrupt raw status bit is set in the per-pin register, the group interrupt status bit is set in gp0_intr1_intr_sts1, the interrupt clears successfully after writing the clear bit, the group interrupt status clears after disabling the group enable, and the sysreg status (raw_stcr1) clears properly.
7. Repeat steps 3-6 for active-low level selection for all 32 GPIO pins.
8. Report PASS if no errors occurred across all 64 interrupt test iterations; report FAIL otherwise.","1. test_case() entry. test_err=0.
2. GIC_EnableIRQ(87) for GPIO0 or GIC_EnableIRQ(88) for GPIO1.
3. write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO0_INTR).
4. Active-high loop i=0..31: wr_val=1<<i; write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(i*4), 0x00180000); wait_on(50); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, wr_val); wait_on(10); write_reg(0xA0243ffc, 0xffffffff); int_pend=1; while(int_pend==1) wait_on(10).
5. Active-low loop i=0..31: write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(i*4), 0x00100000); wait_on(50); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, wr_val); wait_on(10); write_reg(0xA0243ffc, ~(wr_val)); int_pend=1; while(int_pend==1) wait_on(10).
6. Default_IRQHandler(): int_pend=0; write_reg(0xA0243ffc, 0xffffffff); rdata=read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(i*4)); if((rdata & 0x2)!=0x0) SUCCESS else ERROR test_err++; rdata_grp=read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); if((rdata_grp & (1<<i))!=0) SUCCESS else ERROR test_err++; write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(i*4), 0x00110000); wait_on(20); rdata=read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(i*4)); if(rdata==0x100001) SUCCESS else ERROR test_err++; write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, 0x00000000); rdata_grp=read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); if(rdata_grp==0x0) SUCCESS else ERROR test_err++; write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR); rdata=read_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1); if((rdata & LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR)==0) SUCCESS else ERROR test_err++; GIC_ClearIRQ(87).
7. finish(test_err).",gp0_gpio_8; gp0_intr1_intr_en1; gp0_intr1_intr_sts1; intr_en1; raw_stcr1,"MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1; MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1; MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1; 0xA0243ffc","PASS: All 64 interrupt scenarios (32 active-high + 32 active-low) complete without errors. For each GPIO pin: the interrupt raw status bit is set when the level condition is met, the group interrupt status reflects the correct pin, the interrupt clears successfully (register reads back as expected after clear), the group interrupt status clears to zero after disabling, and the sysreg interrupt status clears properly. FAIL: Any of the above checks fails, incrementing the error counter.","In ISR: (1) if((rdata & 0x2)!=0x0) SUCCESS else test_err++. (2) if((rdata_grp & (1<<i))!=0) SUCCESS else test_err++. (3) After clear: if(rdata==0x100001) SUCCESS else test_err++. (4) After group disable: if(rdata_grp==0x0) SUCCESS else test_err++. (5) After sysreg clear: if((rdata & LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR)==0) SUCCESS else test_err++. Final: finish(test_err) where test_err==0 is PASS.",Not,"#include<lss_sysreg.h>; #include<stdio.h>; #include<test_define.c>; #include<test_common.h>; #include<gpio/gpio_def.h>; #include<gpio/gpio_offset.h>",#define CNT 49,"const unsigned long int addr_array[49]={MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10,}; const unsigned int default_value_array[49]={GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_DEFAULT_VAL,}; const unsigned int read_mask_array[49]={GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_READ_MASK,}; const unsigned int write_mask_array[49]={GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_WRITE_MASK,}; const int skip_array[49]={0,0,0,...,0};",TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,"program.c, test_define.c",GPIO